  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Israel does not have right to close UK consulate in Jerusalem, Foreign Office advised",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/28/israel-no-right-close-jerusalem-uk-consulate-foreign-office-advised",
      "description": "<p>Former attorney general Dominic Grieve says Israel is not entitled to shut mission in occupied Palestinian territory</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/28/labour-party-conference-healey-economy-streeting-miliband-andy-burnham-latest-news-updates\">UK politics live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Israel does not have a legal right to act on its plan to close the British consulate in East Jerusalem, the former attorney general Dominic Grieve has advised the UK Foreign Office.</p><p>Israel has said it intends to shut the consulate on 8 October in response to the sweeping ban on trade with goods from Israeli settlements <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/08/uk-accuses-israeli-terrorists-ethnic-cleansing-west-bank-government-backing\">announced by the foreign secretary, Ed Miliband</a>, this month.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/28/israel-no-right-close-jerusalem-uk-consulate-foreign-office-advised\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-28T11:28:12"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘You were right’: Ed Miliband tells critics Labour was wrong on Gaza",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/28/ed-miliband-labour-former-stance-palestine-fell-short",
      "description": "<p>Foreign secretary will tell party’s conference ‘we are not here to accept the status quo but to change it’</p><p>Ed Miliband will tell campaigners and party members who raised the plight of Palestinians they were right that Labour’s approach had not been enough, saying he was heeding the calls of millions of people by imposing sanctions on Israeli settlements.</p><p>The foreign secretary will tell the Labour party conference that the government will take more explicitly progressive foreign policy positions under Andy Burnham, and that the UK will be a leader among like-minded countries in a new age of diplomacy.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/28/ed-miliband-labour-former-stance-palestine-fell-short\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-28T04:00:24"
    }
